<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48217" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">thōrax</span></b> , ācis,
			m. (but f. Treb. Poll.
			<i><span class="en">Claud. 3, 3</span></i>), = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θώραξ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the breast</i>,
				<i>chest</i>, <i>thorax.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, in anatomy, <i><span class="en">Cels. 5,
				25, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 27, 7, 28, §
			49</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A defence</i>, <i>armor</i>, or <i>covering for the breast</i>, <i>a
				breastplate</i>, <i>corselet</i>, <i>cuirass; a doublet</i>, <i>stomacher</i> (syn.
			lorica), <i><span class="en">Liv. 4, 20, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Aug. 82</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 10, 337</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 7, 1,
				1</span></i>.— <i>Dat.</i> thoracibus, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 3,
				87</span></i>.—<i>Gen.</i> thoracum,
					<i><span class="en">Claud. in Ruf. 2,
			260</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A bust</i>, Treb. <i><span class="en">Claud.
				Goth. 3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
